From: OHOS GCC Maintainers <ohos-gcc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] genmatch: Add fflush before fclose for fmemopen compatibility

Some libc implementations (like musl in OpenHarmony/OHOS) have a bug
where fclose() does not properly flush the buffer for fmemopen streams.
This causes the selftest in genmatch to fail because the buffer remains
empty after fclose().

Add an explicit fflush() call before fclose() to work around this issue.

diff --git a/gcc/genmatch.cc b/gcc/genmatch.cc
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/gcc/genmatch.cc
+++ b/gcc/genmatch.cc
@@ -607,6 +607,9 @@ test_diag_vfprintf (const char *expected, const char *msg, ...)
   va_start (ap, msg);
   diag_vfprintf (f, 0, msg, &ap);
   va_end (ap);
+  /* Some libc implementations (e.g., musl) do not flush the buffer on fclose
+     for fmemopen streams, so we need to explicitly flush first.  */
+  fflush (f);
   fclose (f);
   gcc_assert (strcmp (buf, expected) == 0);
 }
